Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override `OnBackButtonPressed` + Custom Toolbar Item

```csharp
// EditProductPage.xaml.cs
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    public EditProductPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior(this, new BackButtonBehavior
        {
            TextOverride = "Cancel",
            Command = new Command(async () => await TryNavigateBack())
        });
    }

    // Handles hardware/OS back button (Android, etc.)
    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            MainThread.BeginInvokeOnMainThread(async () => await TryNavigateBack());
            return true; // cancel default navigation
        }
        return base.OnBackButtonPressed();
    }

    private async Task TryNavigateBack()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave) return;
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }

    // Call this whenever form data changes
    private void OnFormFieldChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
    {
        _hasUnsavedChanges = true;
    }
}
```

## 2. XAML (optional styling)

```xml
<!-- EditProductPage.xaml -->
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Title="Edit Product">
    <!-- Shell.BackButtonBehavior is set in code-behind -->
    <VerticalStackLayout Padding="16">
        <Entry Placeholder="Product Name" TextChanged="OnFormFieldChanged" />
        <!-- ... other fields ... -->
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
```

## Key points

| Concern | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Custom "Cancel" text | `Shell.SetBackButtonBehavior` with `TextOverride` |
| Intercept SW back (toolbar) | `BackButtonBehavior.Command` |
| Intercept HW back (Android) | `OnBackButtonPressed()` returning `true` |
| Confirm dialog | `DisplayAlert` |
| Cancel navigation | Simply don't call `GoToAsync` |

> **Note:** On iOS, swipe-to-go-back isn't intercepted by `OnBackButtonPressed`. If you need to block that gesture too, disable it via a platform-specific handler or set `IsEnabled = false` on the back gesture recognizer in `OnAppearing`.
